@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Still Turn 7: what the current descent settles
+
+The composite original trace source now has an exact complete same-word
+residual-divisor return test. Nine fixed words dividing36 guarantee a strict
+one-step descent whenever the proper rational trace source exists. Every other
+fixed word has infinitely many hard-prime sources where all residual-divisor
+returns fail, even after taking the middle complement. Those primes have
+independent endpoint solutions.
+
+The original missing implication remains: at every hard prime, produce a trace
+source with a nonzero allowed-return coefficient, or produce an original integral
+state directly. Initial trace existence and target compatibility are not
+consequences of the new group-ring observation. Do not enter a witness-guaranteed
+Turn8 under either assumption.
+
+Successful genuinely new arrows relative to the immediate predecessor:
+- Composite a321,R275,u9 at1009 descends to original M a255,R11,u9.
+- p1108801 has two original deletion words21,441; factor7 repairs the residue
+  of the missing factor3. The integer target coefficient2 is not absent modulo2.
+- p51361 requires partial square removal: R8019 ->99 via81. Removing all squares
+  to11 destroys the actual word5 budget.
+- The old p1009,R135,u7436 E rational trace is repaired via its available E
+  complement11, followed by nonsquare deletion45 -> original R3 state.
+
+Permanent negative controls:
+- p29,a14,u2 E complement98 is not even in the relaxed trace domain.
+- Minimal square factor3 fails at p1108801 although the larger available21 works.
+- u8,p48116881,R11999: both original middle orientations have no residual-divisor
+  return; the entire cofactor71 box also fails. No all-shell failure is asserted.
+- Fixed-modulus prime progressions in the certificate are reduced classes, not
+  lists of independently certified prime values.
+
+A new global arrow must exploit a family of sources at the same prescribed p,
+change the word beyond the present complement, use a justified non-divisor
+residual, or prove a positive coefficient in the complete source. The present
+infinite counterfamily rules out simply assuming that arbitrary proper traces
+always descend through their residual divisors.
diff --git a/research/incoming/es-turn07-divisor-descent-20260921/MORPHISMS.md b/research/incoming/es-turn07-divisor-descent-20260921/MORPHISMS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c17820b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/incoming/es-turn07-divisor-descent-20260921/MORPHISMS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Explicit maps, domains, fibres and information loss
+
+1. Original square-divisor box: f_l in [0,2v_l(a)] -> u=product l^f_l.
+   Inverse f_l=v_l(u). The centred beta is f_l-v_l(a).
+2. Original u and E/M tag -> rational ordered triples in equations (1)-(2).
+   The full original reciprocal identity holds before integrality. First-trace
+   integrality is the squared gate, not the full gate.
+3. Rational trace tails -> b=Ry-pa,c=Rz-pa, bc=(pa)^2. The p-valuation pair
+   recovers E canonical orientation or either M orientation and original u.
+4. Trace source -> d=R/gcd(R,G). The exact common tail denominator is d and
+   d^2|R. A supported rational trace is not an original integer hit when d>1.
+5. Original budget u|a^2 <-> K(u)|a <-> p+R=0 mod m=4K(u).
+6. Complete divisor-removal domain: k|R, d|k, k=1 mod m.
+   Return R'=R/k,a'=(p+R')/4,u'=u. A proper input strictly decreases a.
+7. Target normalization: gcd(a',u) gives h',r',s' and the original quotient
+   kappa' or lambda'. Both ordered reciprocal identities and inverses are checked.
+   Old and new factor inventories differ; their beta vectors change by
+   v_l(a)-v_l(a'), including all zero coordinates.
+8. Complete inverse fibres: retain k, or enumerate k <= (p-1)/R' satisfying
+   k=1 mod m, R'k|G^2, R'k not dividing G. Distinct source-to-target records
+   are not identified before this actual pushforward.
+9. Coefficient pushforward from divisors of R/d into (Z/m)^*: geometric prime
+   factors, not binomial coloured occurrences. Coefficient at d^{-1} counts
+   the entire removal set. The kernel is the original same-target differences.
+10. Square subdomain R=delta*t^2, q0=K(d), q0|q|t, q^2=1 mod m. Its inverse
+    reads q=sqrt(k). The squarefree part delta is not the radical and can share
+    prime factors with t.
+11. Square-image coefficient polynomial: divisors v of t/q0 -> v^2 mod m.
+    Coefficient at q0^{-2} counts square deletions. Original exponent vectors
+    and any repeated residue multiplicities remain attached.
+12. Shortest completion: an identity subword can be deleted from the actual
+    remaining divisor. It bounds a word already known to exist, and is not
+    a target-occupancy theorem.
+13. Complement u -> a^2/u: always a relaxed M map and swaps the tails. At E its
+    exact relaxed-gate domain is K(R)|(p^2-1). The flag and old a invert it.
+    At a fixed E word u=a do not invent a second original word.
+14. Uniform square-image collapse happens exactly at m|24, equivalently u|36.
+    The integer coefficient there is tau(t/q0), not its reduction modulo two.
+15. Counterfamily CRT returns p congruences, not an arbitrary chosen prime.
+    Dirichlet is used only after proving reducedness. Keep u,m,b,delta,t,e,L,
+    residue, modulus and a lower threshold. Intermediate numerical residues in
+    the finite construction table are not asserted prime.
+16. Counterfamily M complement budget: K(a^2/u)=a/B(u). Its modulus exceeds R;
+    the original word box is what obstructs every residual-divisor return.
+17. Cofactor-delta box is Div(((delta+1)/4)^2), NOT the original residual-delta
+    shell Div(((p+delta)/4)^2). Empty cofactor capacity does not identify them.
+18. Independent endpoint returns recover valid E/M states at each counterfamily
+    prime. The counterfamily is not a family of ES counterexamples.
diff --git a/research/incoming/es-turn07-divisor-descent-20260921/README.md b/research/incoming/es-turn07-divisor-descent-20260921/README.md
